`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Just-In-Time Provisioning (JITP) mode delegates provisioning to AWS instead of the connector doing it directly. When the connector detects the DMS is in ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"jitp"})," mode, it creates a JITP provisioning template in AWS IoT Core and attaches it to the registered CA certificate. The ",e.jsx(t.del,{className:"lm-diff-del",children:"template is created when the DMS is created in Lamassu, not at device enrollment, and it is not updated afterwards (see the notice below). From then on"}),e.jsxs(t.ins,{className:"lm-diff-ins",children:["connector attempts to create this template when the DMS is created and again on every full DMS edit (",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"PUT /v1/dms/{id}"}),") — not at device enrollment time. The attempt is not idempotent: when a template named after the DMS ID already exists, the creation call fails, the event is retried three times and finally lands in the ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"lamassu-dlq"})," poison queue (see "]}),e.jsx(t.a,{href:"/docs/platform/iot-fleets/integrations/aws-iot-core#troubleshooting",children:e.jsx(t.ins,{className:"lm-diff-ins",children:"Troubleshooting"})}),e.jsxs(t.ins,{className:"lm-diff-ins",children:["). The template is created once; later DMS edits never update its content. A DMS update that omits ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"metadata"})," or sends ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"null"})," keeps the stored metadata, so the connector key ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"lamassu.io/iot/{connector_id}"})," remains present and the attempt is still triggered. A body that supplies a ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"metadata"})," object replaces the stored metadata entirely: if that object does not carry the connector key, the key is dropped and the connector silently skips the DMS's future events. Once the template is attached"]}),", when a device with a certificate issued by that CA connects to AWS IoT Core for the first time, AWS executes the template automatically: it creates the Thing, registers the certificate and activates it."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(a,{type:"warn",title:"Editing a DMS in JITP mode does not update the AWS template",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The connector creates the template, named after the DMS ID, only once. Each later edit of the DMS that keeps the connector key tries to create it again and fails, because the connector does not update existing templates. Later changes to ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"jitp_config.provisioning_role_arn"}),", ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"jitp_config.enable_template"})," or to the groups and policies the template references must be applied by hand in AWS IoT Core."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The failed event is retried and ends in ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"lamassu-dlq"}),". Groups and policies are registered before the failure, but the assignment of the template to the registered CA, the write-back of the ARN to the DMS and the shadow update when ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"ManagedCAs"})," changes are skipped."]})]}),`
